    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "IMPERIAL AIRLINES\nEMBRAER EMB-110P1 BANDEIRANTE\nEMERGENCY PROCEDURES\n(PLEASE DO NOT REMOVE THIS CARD FROM AIRCRAFT)\nWHERE TO FIND YOUR LIFE VEST\nLife vests are located in a holder under\neach seat. Do not remove the life vest from\nthe sealed bag unless actually necessary.\nHOW TO USE YOUR LIFE VEST\nA Put on life vest over head.\nB Wrap straps around waist and tie in front.\nC AFTER YOU LEAVE AIRCRAFT, jerk gas\nrelease knobs.\nD If later the vest becomes too soft, it may\nbe inflated orally.\nWHAT TO DO IN CASE OF AN EMERGENCY LANDING\nRemain calm and follow instructions of crew. Sit well\nback in seat - pull seat belt tight - assume appropriate\nposition in illustration until plane stops. When airplane is\ncomplete stopped, unfasten seat belt and follow instruc-\nAIR STAIR DOOR (A)\n1. PRESS LOCK\n2. PULL HANDLE\n3. PUSH DOOR\n2.\nFRONT EMERGENCY EXIT (B)\nIN EMERGENCY\n1. PULL RING AND REMOVE COVER\n2. LIFT HANDLE AND PUSH DOOR\n3. PULL SAFETY LATCH RING DOWN\n2.\n1100\n3.\nEmergency\nExits\nOVERWING EMERGENCY EXITS (C)\nEMERGENCY EXIT\n1. TEAR OFF COVER\n2. PULL HANDLE\n3. PUSH DOOR\nA Fire Extinguisher\n2.",
      "PLEASE OBSERVE\n\"NO SMOKING\" SIGN\nIt is an Imperial policy to\nrequest that all passengers\nrefrain from smoking aboard\nthe aircraft. We thank you for\nyour cooperation in this matter.\nPLEASE FASTEN\nSEAT BELTS BEFORE\nTAKEOFF AND LANDING\nAt takeoff and landing, seat\nbelts should be fastened. At\nthese times, the \"Fasten Seat\nBelt\" sign will be lighted. In\nbumpy air, the sign will be\nlighted during flight. There is\nno cause for alarm but we ask\nthat you comply for a more\ncomfortable ride. When the\nsign is off, your belt may be\nreleased.\nHOW TO USE FIRE EXTINGUISHER\n1. Remove from clip.\n3. Direct nozzle to base of flame.\n2. Remove safety pin.\n4. Squeeze handle to discharge.\nDO NOT REMOVE FROM AIRPLANE\nFEDERAL LAWS REQUIRE THIS CARD BE KEPT IN THE SEAT POCKET\nFOR PASSENGER INFORMATION\n2002.127.337"
    ],
